data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/mission-report.md\", \"content\": \"# Campaign csrclkey — mission \\\"greet, tested\\\" — report\\n\\n## Outcome: met\\n\\nAll three mission criteria satisfied:\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` defines `greet(name)` returning `f\\\"Hello, {name}!\\\"`.\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` covers a normal name (`greet(\\\"Alice\\\") == \\\"Hello, Alice!\\\"`)\\n   and the empty string (`greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`).\\n3. `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exits 0 (2 tests, OK).\\n\\n## Process\\n\\n- Dispatched the task to `dev` (dispatch d002) with the exact deliverables and\\n  a request to run the test suite and paste its output.\\n- `dev` implemented both files, ran the suite successfully, and committed to\\n  its branch `cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>` (commit `5bd6bd4`,\\n  \\\"Add greet function with tests\\\").\\n- Judged by fetching `refs/remotes/campaign/dev/subject` and independently\\n  re-running `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` in a detached worktree\\n  checked out from that ref (not relying on dev's self-report). Result: 2\\n  tests, OK, exit code 0. Source inspected directly and matches spec exactly.\\n- Accepted dev's work (d002) on first attempt — no rework needed.\\n\\n## Branch state\\n\\n- Orchestrator branch (`cs-sandbox/<ORCHESTRATOR:1>.<GROUP:1>`):\\n  no source changes — orchestrator wrote no code, per its role. Dispatch/plan/\\n  assessment files were placed in this campaign's own tooling (send/note),\\n  not as repo commits.\\n- dev branch: `cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>` @ `5bd6bd4`, tree\\n  differs from base, contains exactly the two required files.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":0,"type":"content_block_delta"}

